    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d370">

                <pb facs="0753" n="719" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v15p1/pg719"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">695A.0024/12–2952</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Director of the
                        Office of United Nations Political and Security Affairs
                        (Wainhouse)</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d370-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            type="conversation-or-meeting-date" when="1952-12-29">December 29,
                            1952</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>Subject:</label>
                    <item>Korea: Prisoners of War.</item>
                </list>
                <list subtype="participants" type="description">
                    <label>Participants:</label>
                    <item>Mr. John Foster Dulles</item>
                    <item>Mr. David W. Wainhouse</item>
                </list>
                <pb facs="0754" n="720" xml:id="pg720"/>
                <p>In a conversation the other day which I had with Mr. Dulles, he referred to a
                    visit paid him in New York by Mr. Krishna Menon of the Indian Delegation. Mr.
                    Dulles said that Mr. Menon sought to secure concessions from him on the American
                    stand on the prisoner of war question. Mr. Dulles said that he gave no
                    encouragement whatsoever to Mr. Menon on this matter.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">David W.
                    Wainhouse</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d370-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d370-f1-content">
                <p>Copies of this memorandum went to Bruce, Matthews, Hickerson, Allison, Johnson,
                    and Henkin.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
